# Syncthing

## sync2proton 

Mirrors Syncthing's ~/sync/ directory to Proton Drive's ~/Proton Drive/Backups/sync/ directory on a schedule.

### How it works

- Syncthing owns ~/sync/ and handles real-time device sync
- This agent runs rsync hourly, mirroring ~/sync/ to ~/PROTON_DRIVE/Backups/sync/
- Proton Drive versions each changed file automatically on receipt
- vim artifacts and Syncthing internals are excluded from the mirror

### Directory layout

| Path                         | Role                                       gg                              |
|------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| ~/sync/                      | Syncthing root — source of truth, do not edit files in the Proton mirror |
| ~/PROTON_DRIVE/Backups/sync/ | rsync mirror — read-only backup target, managed by this agent            |

### Prerequisites

- Syncthing installed and ~/sync/ configured with desired subfolders. Handled in Brewfile.
- Proton Drive desktop app installed with ~/Proton Drive/ mounted
- rsync available at /usr/bin/rsync (macOS ships this)

### Environment variables (set in ~/.localrc, not committed)

| Variable             | Description                                                                            |
|----------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `SYNCTHING_ROOT`     | Absolute path to Syncthing watched root, e.g. `$HOME/sync`                             |
| `PROTON_BACKUP_DEST` | Absolute path to Proton Drive backup target — find it via `ls ~/Library/CloudStorage/` |
| `SSD_VOLUME`         | Absolute path to SSD volume, e.g. `/Volumes/SSD`                                       |
| `SSD_BACKUP_DEST`    | Absolute path to SSD backup target, e.g. `/Volumes/SSD/Backups/sync`                   |
